        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b6de7f8-b4eb-51f3-8321-76fd22140e78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bangor Air National Guard Base, Bangor International Airport, Dow Air Force Base, Bangor, Maine\n- Organizations: United States Air National Guard, Maine Air National Guard, 101st Air Refueling Wing, 776th Radar Squadron, Northeast Air Defense Sector, Air Combat Command\n\nFacts:\n- Bangor Air National Guard Base is a United States Air National Guard base.\n- In 1968, the base was sold to the city of Bangor, Maine, and became Bangor International Airport.\n- In the late 1960s, most Air Force aircraft and personnel left Bangor International Airport.\n- Bangor International Airport was formerly a military installation known as Dow Air Force Base.\n- Bangor International Airport has continued to host Maine Air National Guard units, including the 101st Air Refueling Wing.\n- The 776th Radar Squadron was last assigned to the Northeast Air Defense Sector under Air Combat Command and was stationed at Bangor Air National Guard Base, Maine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
